  "lines": [
    {
      "id": "bathsheba_0",
      "cite": "2 Samuel 11:3",
      "items": [
        {
          "id": "bathsheba_0_text",
          "type": "text",
          "sfx": false,
          "text": "In the spring, when kings go out to battle, David stayed in Jerusalem and walked on his roof. From there he saw a woman bathing, and he sent to learn who she was.",
          "position": "middle-left",
          "margin": "M",
          "delay": 800,
          "visibleDuration": 0,
          "entryFx": "fade",
          "exitFx": "fade",
          "style": "comic",
          "bold": false,
          "italic": false,
          "rotation": 0,
          "font": "default",
          "fontSize": 0,
          "speaker": "narrator",
          "align": "left",
          "width": "1/2",
          "zIndex": 1
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "bathsheba_1",
      "items": [
        {
          "id": "bathsheba_1_text",
          "type": "text",
          "sfx": false,
          "text": "She was Bathsheba, the wife of Uriah the Hittite, one of David's own mighty men. David took her, and the child she carried was his.",
          "position": "center",
          "margin": "M",
          "delay": 800,
          "visibleDuration": 0,
          "entryFx": "fade",
          "exitFx": "fade",
          "style": "comic",
          "bold": false,
          "italic": false,
          "rotation": 0,
          "font": "default",
          "fontSize": 0,
          "speaker": "narrator",
          "align": "center",
          "width": "1/2",
          "zIndex": 1
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "bathsheba_2",
      "items": [
        {
          "id": "bathsheba_2_text",
          "type": "text",
          "sfx": false,
          "text": "Send for Uriah. Let him come to me and sleep in his own house. Then we will know whether the child is his.",
          "position": "middle-left",
          "margin": "M",
          "delay": 800,
          "visibleDuration": 0,
          "entryFx": "fade",
          "exitFx": "fade",
          "style": "comic",
          "bold": false,
          "italic": false,
          "rotation": 0,
          "font": "default",
          "fontSize": 0,
          "speaker": "david",
          "align": "left",
          "width": "1/2",
          "zIndex": 1
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "bathsheba_3",
      "cite": "2 Samuel 11:11",
      "items": [
        {
          "id": "bathsheba_3_text",
          "type": "text",
          "sfx": false,
          "text": "Uriah came. He would not eat or sleep in his own house while his comrades fought under the walls of Rabbah. The king's plan would not work.",
          "position": "center",
          "margin": "M",
          "delay": 800,
          "visibleDuration": 0,
          "entryFx": "fade",
          "exitFx": "fade",
          "style": "comic",
          "bold": false,
          "italic": false,
          "rotation": 0,
          "font": "default",
          "fontSize": 0,
          "speaker": "narrator",
          "align": "center",
          "width": "1/2",
          "zIndex": 1
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "bathsheba_4",
      "items": [
        {
          "id": "bathsheba_4_text",
          "type": "text",
          "sfx": false,
          "text": "Put Uriah at the front of the fight. Let the fiercest men surround him. Then retreat and leave him exposed.",
          "position": "middle-left",
          "margin": "M",
          "delay": 800,
          "visibleDuration": 0,
          "entryFx": "fade",
          "exitFx": "fade",
          "style": "comic",
          "bold": false,
          "italic": false,
          "rotation": 0,
          "font": "default",
          "fontSize": 0,
          "speaker": "david",
          "align": "left",
          "width": "1/2",
          "zIndex": 1
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "bathsheba_5",
      "audioSfx": "assets/audio/sfx/camp_fire.mp3",
      "cite": "2 Samuel 11:25",
      "items": [
        {
          "id": "bathsheba_5_text",
          "type": "text",
          "sfx": false,
          "text": "Uriah fell and was killed. The messenger ran to David with the news, and the king said nothing at all. The city kept its silence.",
          "position": "center",
          "margin": "M",
          "delay": 800,
          "visibleDuration": 0,
          "entryFx": "fade",
          "exitFx": "fade",
          "style": "comic",
          "bold": false,
          "italic": false,
          "rotation": 0,
          "font": "default",
          "fontSize": 0,
          "speaker": "narrator",
          "align": "center",
          "width": "1/2",
          "zIndex": 1
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "bathsheba_6",
      "cite": "2 Samuel 12:18",
      "items": [
        {
          "id": "bathsheba_6_text",
          "type": "text",
          "sfx": false,
          "text": "The child born to Bathsheba fell ill and died within days. David held the infant and wept, but he could not undo what had been done.",
          "position": "center",
          "margin": "M",
          "delay": 800,
          "visibleDuration": 0,
          "entryFx": "fade",
          "exitFx": "fade",
          "style": "comic",
          "bold": false,
          "italic": false,
          "rotation": 0,
          "font": "default",
          "fontSize": 0,
          "speaker": "narrator",
          "align": "center",
          "width": "1/2",
          "zIndex": 1
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "bathsheba_7",
      "items": [
        {
          "id": "bathsheba_7_text",
          "type": "text",
          "sfx": false,
          "text": "The most dangerous thing a king can do is use his power to make a wrong thing look like a right one. The roof was only a roof until he looked from it.",
          "position": "center",
          "margin": "M",
          "delay": 800,
          "visibleDuration": 0,
          "entryFx": "bounce",
          "exitFx": "fade",
